---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/okad-house.css';
---

<Base title="Video Ads for Mobile Apps — User Acquisition Creative | OKAD" description="Video ad production for mobile apps and SaaS. Screen recordings, creator walkthroughs, hook testing for Meta and TikTok campaigns.">
  <div class="okh">

    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="khero" style="padding:80px 0 48px">
      <div class="w" style="max-width:900px">
        <span class="kick">Video Ads for Mobile Apps & SaaS</span>
        <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.2rem);margin-bottom:16px">App Install Ads That <span class="cap">Beat Creative Fatigue</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">Mobile app user acquisition is a creative volume game. Your best-performing ad will fatigue in 7-14 days, your audience pools are narrower than e-commerce, and every competitor is fighting for the same install. You need a steady pipeline of fresh concepts across multiple formats — screen recordings, creator walkthroughs, motion graphics, and UGC — to keep cost-per-install down and install rates climbing.</p>
        <div class="row" style="margin-top:24px">
          <a class="btn" href="https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="mailto:olga@okad.agency">Email us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHY APPS NEED CREATIVE TESTING -->
    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:16px">Why Apps Need <span class="cap g">Creative Testing</span></h2>
      <p style="color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);margin-bottom:24px">Mobile app UA has always been a creative game, but the rules got harder. Privacy changes killed precise targeting, algorithms rely on creative signals to find users, and CPIs have climbed 30-40% across most verticals since 2023. The brands winning the install race are the ones producing the most testable creative, fastest.</p>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:16px">
        <div style="padding:24px;background:#f4f9e8;border-radius:12px">
          <h3 style="font-size:17px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--dark,#111)">Ad Fatigue Hits Faster</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">App audiences are smaller and more defined than broad e-commerce audiences. That means frequency spikes quicker — your users see the same ad three or four times in a week instead of once. When frequency crosses 2.5 on Meta, click-through rates drop by 30-50% and cost-per-install inflates rapidly. The only defense is a constant rotation of fresh creative that gives the algorithm new signals to optimize against.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:#f3e5f5;border-radius:12px">
          <h3 style="font-size:17px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--dark,#111)">Hooks Matter More</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">You have a 1.5-second attention window on mobile feeds. For app ads specifically, users need to understand what your app does and why they should care before their thumb keeps scrolling. Every frame in the first two seconds must earn the next second of watch time. Generic intros like "Are you looking for..." burn through 40% of your hook window before saying anything meaningful. The hook is the ad — everything after it is cleanup.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:#e1f5fe;border-radius:12px">
          <h3 style="font-size:17px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--dark,#111)">Format Diversity Wins</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">Single-format creative strategies plateau fast. Brands running only UGC or only motion graphics hit an effectiveness ceiling within 3-4 weeks. Mixing screen recordings with creator walkthroughs, layering UGC over animated feature callouts, and alternating between problem-solution and social proof formats gives the algorithm distinct creative clusters to test. Our data shows that multi-format campaigns sustain performance 2-3x longer than single-format approaches.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:#f6f5f4;border-radius:12px">
          <h3 style="font-size:17px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--dark,#111)">Platform-Specific Creative</h3>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">What works on TikTok fails on Meta, and what wins on Meta underperforms on YouTube. TikTok rewards raw, trend-driven content where the app feels like a discovery. Meta rewards clear value propositions and structured hooks. YouTube pre-roll needs to survive the 5-second skip window. Repurposing the same asset across platforms is lazy and expensive — you pay full CPM for creative that was never designed for that environment.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CONTENT TYPES -->
    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:8px">Content Types We <span class="cap y">Produce</span></h2>
      <p style="color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);margin-bottom:24px">Each format serves a different stage of the user journey and performs differently across platforms. We produce all of them so your creative mix stays diverse.</p>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:16px">
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">Screen Recording + Voiceover</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">Clean screen captures showing your app in action with professional narration explaining what the user is seeing. We record on actual devices (not emulators) to capture authentic scroll speed, tap animations, and loading states. The voiceover follows a benefit-first script: we lead with what the feature does for the user, not how it works technically. Screen recordings consistently rank among the top-performing formats for apps with strong UI because they answer the question "what will I actually get?" before the install.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">Creator Walkthrough</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">A real person on camera using your app, reacting to features, and sharing their genuine experience. The creator films themselves holding the phone, with their screen captured separately and composited in post. This format bridges the trust gap — it shows the app is real, usable, and valued by someone the viewer can relate to. Creator walkthroughs outperform pure screen recordings by 20-35% on TikTok because they add a human layer that feels native to the platform rather than like an advertisement.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">Problem-Solution</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">The most reliable app ad structure: open with a pain point the viewer recognizes, agitate it for 3-5 seconds, then reveal your app as the solution. The hook names the problem directly — "I used to spend 45 minutes every morning planning meals" — and the payoff shows the app eliminating that friction. We script these around real user complaints pulled from app store reviews and Reddit threads, so the pain point always resonates. Problem-solution ads have the highest conversion rates for apps solving a clear, specific problem.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">Trending Format / Meme-Style</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">Leveraging current TikTok and Reels trends with your app woven in naturally. We monitor trending sounds, formats, and meme templates daily and identify which ones can be adapted for app promotion without feeling forced. A trending format ad has a 48-72 hour window where it outperforms everything else, so speed matters. We maintain a rapid-fire production pipeline that can turn around trend-based ads within 24 hours. These ads drive the lowest CPMs because platforms actively boost content that uses trending elements.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">Motion Graphics Explainer</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">Animated feature highlights for complex apps where a screen recording alone would confuse viewers. Motion graphics let us simplify multi-step workflows, visualize data transformations, and highlight UI elements with callouts and zoom effects that guide the viewer's eye. For fintech, health-tech, and productivity apps with dense interfaces, motion graphics reduce cognitive load and help viewers understand the value proposition in under 15 seconds. We produce these in 9:16 and 4:5 with bold text overlays optimized for sound-off viewing.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">Comparison / Before-After</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">Split-screen or sequential format showing life without your app versus life with it. The "before" state needs to feel genuinely frustrating — scattered notes, missed workouts, confusing spreadsheets — and the "after" must feel like an obvious upgrade. We film both states with the same creator to maintain continuity and credibility. Before-after ads work especially well for habit-tracking, fitness, finance, and productivity apps because the transformation is visual and immediate. This format also allows side-by-side competitor comparisons when positioned carefully.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- OUR WORK -->
    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:16px">Our <span class="cap p">Work</span></h2>
      <p style="color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);margin-bottom:24px">We have produced over 160 ads for a single AI productivity app in four months, turning a creative-starved account into a testing machine. Here is how we approach app creative at scale.</p>

      <div style="padding:32px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6);margin-bottom:24px">
        <h3 style="font-size:17px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--dark,#111)">The Approach: Weekly Creative Sprints</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 12px">Instead of producing a batch of 20 ads and waiting a month to see results, we run weekly creative sprints. Each sprint focuses on testing a specific hypothesis — a new hook angle, a different creator demographic, a format variation, or a messaging pivot. We produce 8-12 variations per sprint, launch them into structured testing campaigns, and review performance data within 5-7 days. Winners get scaled with variations (new hooks on the same body, same hook with different creators, extended cuts for retargeting). Losers get analyzed for learnings that inform the next sprint. This loop means the account never runs out of fresh creative and every dollar of ad spend generates data that makes the next batch better.</p>
        <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin:0">The result: one in three test videos brought customers at or below the target CPI. The single best-performing ad we produced cost 35% less per customer than the account average and earned the largest daily budget allocation among approximately 770 active ads in the account.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:16px">
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:15px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">AI Productivity App</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">160+ ads produced across 4 months. Tested 70 concepts in the first batch alone, with 14 reaching winner status. Formats ranged from screen recordings showing AI features to creator reaction videos and problem-solution scripts built around real user reviews. Reduced cost-per-install by 35% on the best-performing ads compared to the client's previous creative.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:15px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">Language Learning App</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">Produced 60+ video ads combining creator walkthroughs with screen recordings showing real lesson flows. Tested hooks around "learn in 5 minutes a day" vs "stop forgetting what you learn" vs social proof from user milestones. The problem-solution format outperformed all others by 40%, and creator walkthroughs in the target language drove 25% higher install rates than English-only versions.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:15px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin-bottom:8px">Fitness Tracker App</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.6;margin:0">Built a library of 45+ ads mixing workout screen recordings, creator transformation testimonials, and before-after format ads. Discovered that showing the app during actual workouts (not staged demos) increased thumb-stop rate by 50%. Motion graphics explaining the tracking algorithm outperformed feature-list ads by 3x on Meta, while raw UGC dominated on TikTok.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- THE APP CREATIVE PLAYBOOK -->
    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:16px">The App Creative <span class="cap v">Playbook</span></h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom:32px">
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--dark,#111)">The Creative Testing Loop</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px">Every successful app creative program follows the same loop: Concept, Produce, Test, Learn, Iterate. The difference between teams that scale and teams that stall is how fast they move through this loop and how rigorously they extract learnings from each cycle.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px"><strong>Concept (Days 1-2):</strong> Start with 8-10 hypotheses, not scripts. A hypothesis is a testable statement like "showing the AI output before showing the input will increase hook rate" or "female creators 25-34 will outperform male creators for this audience." Each hypothesis maps to one or more ad variations.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px"><strong>Produce (Days 3-5):</strong> Script and shoot 2-3 variations per hypothesis. Keep production lean — the goal is testable creative, not polished content. Screen recordings take hours, not days. Creator shoots follow tight briefs with clear deliverables.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px"><strong>Test (Days 6-12):</strong> Launch into structured testing campaigns with $20-50 per ad per day. Use CBO or ABO depending on the platform and test structure. Every ad gets at least $100-150 in spend before a kill decision — anything less and the data is noise.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px"><strong>Learn (Day 13):</strong> Pull performance data and categorize every ad as winner (below CPI target), viable (within 20% of target), or loser (above 20% of target). Analyze what the winners share: hook type, creator demographic, format, messaging angle, length. Document these patterns — they are the foundation for the next sprint.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7"><strong>Iterate (Days 14+):</strong> Take the winning patterns and produce 5-10 variations. Change one variable at a time: same hook with a different creator, same creator with a different hook, same concept in a different format. This is where you scale winners without killing what made them work.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom:32px">
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--dark,#111)">Hook Frameworks That Work for App Installs</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px">The hook is the single most important variable in any app install ad. We test five hook frameworks and rotate between them to prevent audience fatigue:</p>
        <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:24px;display:grid;gap:12px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7">
          <li><strong>Curiosity Gap:</strong> "I found an app that does something I didn't think was possible." This hook works because it creates an open loop the viewer needs to close. Best for apps with a genuinely novel feature. Average thumb-stop rate: 35-45%.</li>
          <li><strong>Social Proof:</strong> "2 million people are using this app and I finally tried it." Leverages herd behavior and reduces perceived risk. Works best when you have real download numbers or recognizable user milestones to reference. Drives 15-20% higher install rates than curiosity hooks on average.</li>
          <li><strong>Problem Callout:</strong> "If you still [painful manual process], you need to see this." Directly names the pain the viewer is experiencing. Strongest for productivity, finance, and health apps where the problem is daily and tangible. This hook has the highest correlation with post-install retention because it attracts users who actually need the solution.</li>
          <li><strong>Shocking Stat:</strong> "The average person wastes 2.5 hours a day on [activity this app fixes]." Numbers stop the scroll because they are concrete and falsifiable. The stat must be real and sourced — fabricated statistics erode trust and trigger comment-section pushback that tanks ad performance.</li>
          <li><strong>Before/After:</strong> "Here's my [workflow/routine] before this app vs after." Visual transformation hooks that show a clear upgrade. Strongest in the first three seconds when the "before" state is genuinely chaotic and the "after" is clean and satisfying. Works across all platforms but performs best on Instagram Reels.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom:32px">
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--dark,#111)">Why Most App Install Ads Fail</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px">After producing thousands of app ads and seeing the performance data, we have identified the four most common failure patterns:</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px"><strong>Too long:</strong> The optimal length for app install ads on TikTok is 15-25 seconds. On Meta, 20-35 seconds. On YouTube Shorts, 30-45 seconds. Anything over 45 seconds needs a very strong reason to exist — and "we have a lot of features" is not that reason. Every second past the optimal window costs you completions and conversions.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px"><strong>Feature-focused instead of benefit-focused:</strong> "Our app has AI-powered scheduling with calendar sync and smart notifications" means nothing to a viewer. "This app plans your entire week in 30 seconds" means everything. Features are what the engineering team built. Benefits are what the user's life looks like after using it. Every sentence in the ad should pass the "so what?" test.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px"><strong>No clear CTA:</strong> "Download now" is a CTA but it is not a good one. "Try it free — link in bio" is better. "The free version does everything I just showed you" is best. The CTA needs to lower the perceived commitment: free trial, no credit card, delete it if you hate it. App installs are impulse decisions and the CTA should feel effortless.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7"><strong>One ad, one chance:</strong> Running a single "hero" ad and hoping it works is the most expensive way to fail. Even the best creative teams have a 20-30% win rate. That means you need to produce and test 10 ads to find 2-3 that work. Brands that produce one polished video per month will always lose to brands that produce 10 scrappy variations per week.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;margin-bottom:12px;color:var(--dark,#111)">Scaling Winners: 10+ Variations from One Concept</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px">When you find a winning ad, the instinct is to increase its budget. That works for a week — maybe two. Then performance degrades as the audience saturates. The smarter move is to create variations that preserve the winning elements while refreshing the creative signal.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:12px">Here is how we generate 10+ variations from a single winning concept:</p>
        <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:24px;display:grid;gap:10px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7">
          <li><strong>Hook swap:</strong> Keep the body and CTA, test 3-4 different hooks. If the original hook was curiosity-based, try a social proof version and a problem callout version.</li>
          <li><strong>Creator swap:</strong> Same script, different creator. Age, gender, and creator style all affect performance differently across audience segments. A winning script with a new face resets creative fatigue.</li>
          <li><strong>Format swap:</strong> Convert a creator walkthrough into a screen recording + voiceover version, or layer the creator footage over motion graphics. Same message, different visual treatment.</li>
          <li><strong>Length variations:</strong> Cut a 30-second winner into a 15-second version for TikTok and extend it to 45 seconds for YouTube. Each length hits a different audience behavior pattern.</li>
          <li><strong>Platform adaptation:</strong> Reframe the 9:16 version for 4:5 (Meta feed), 1:1 (Instagram feed), and 16:9 (YouTube pre-roll). Aspect ratio changes require re-compositing, not just cropping.</li>
          <li><strong>CTA variations:</strong> Test "download free" vs "try it today" vs "link in bio" vs "tap to install." CTA wording changes can swing conversion rates by 10-20%.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- OUR PROCESS -->
    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:24px">Our <span class="cap g">Process</span></h2>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:20px">
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted,#8e8e8e);letter-spacing:0.05em">01</span>
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin:8px 0 6px">App Audit & Competitive Analysis</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.5;margin:0">We download your app, use it extensively, and study every competitor ad running on Meta Ad Library and TikTok Creative Center. We analyze your app store reviews (both yours and competitors') to find the language real users use to describe their problems and wins. This research surfaces the messaging angles, hook styles, and formats most likely to resonate with your target audience.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted,#8e8e8e);letter-spacing:0.05em">02</span>
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin:8px 0 6px">Concept & Script Development</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.5;margin:0">We write hook-first scripts for 8-12 ad concepts per sprint. Every script starts with the hook — the first 1.5 seconds — and builds backward from there. We develop scripts across multiple formats (screen recording, creator walkthrough, problem-solution, motion graphics) so the testing batch covers diverse creative signals. Each script includes shot-by-shot direction, voiceover or dialogue, and text overlay placement.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted,#8e8e8e);letter-spacing:0.05em">03</span>
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin:8px 0 6px">Production Sprint</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.5;margin:0">Screen captures are recorded on real devices with clean demo accounts. Creator shoots are managed through our network of 600+ vetted creators who receive detailed briefs with reference examples. Motion graphics are produced in-house with native mobile aspect ratios and bold typography for sound-off viewing. Everything is edited with platform-native pacing — fast cuts for TikTok, structured storytelling for Meta, retention-optimized openings for YouTube.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:24px;background:var(--off-white,#f7f7f7);border-radius:12px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e6e6e6)">
          <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted,#8e8e8e);letter-spacing:0.05em">04</span>
          <strong style="display:block;font-size:17px;color:var(--dark,#111);margin:8px 0 6px">Performance Review & Next Sprint</strong>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--soft,#4d4d49);line-height:1.5;margin:0">After 5-7 days of spend, we pull performance data and categorize every ad: winner, viable, or loser. We analyze what the winners share — hook type, creator profile, format, length, messaging angle — and document patterns in a shared creative playbook. These insights directly shape the next sprint's concepts. Winners get scaled with variations (hook swaps, creator swaps, format swaps). The cycle repeats weekly or bi-weekly depending on your budget and velocity goals.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
